{
	"_doc": "Stub animations of a fight (v0.8.4.23, docs/design/systems/combat-animations.md). A kind is played phase by phase: windup at the doer, travel from the doer to the target (looped while it flies), hit at the target, the area or the path, fade. Each phase is a stub of game/ui/anims/stub_anim.gd until a real one replaces it: `frames` — a SpriteFrames .tres whose animation named after a phase plays instead of that phase stub (the others stay stubs); `scene` — a .tscn whose root extends FightAnim plays the whole kind. A state is drawn on the token on every redraw: `texture` is its overlay. `time` is seconds at the normal speed of a fight.",
